From 9ffb767150e960b5e119d733fa42ac33e3cf46a7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sebastian Werner <swernerx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 20:42:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] perf(parser): measure each container line's indentation and
 end once
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The list item collector and the block quote walk asked the same
questions of every line they consumed — where it ends, where the next
one starts, how deeply it is indented, whether it is blank, and what
follows that indentation — and every answer came from its own scan over
the same bytes. An indented list continuation line was walked by
`trim`, by `calc_indentation` and by `push_line_without_indent`, and
walked again by `trim_start` or `first_non_whitespace_in_line` once it
turned out to carry a marker or to continue a paragraph lazily; a
blank-line lookahead re-measured the very line it had just scanned; a
quote line walked its prefix for the blank test and again for the
marker's column arithmetic.

`LineFacts` now produces all of that from one terminator search plus
one walk of the leading whitespace, and both collectors hand the facts
down. `push_line_without_indent` takes the measured run, so a tab-free
indent dedents by slicing instead of walking, and `line_starts_block`
takes the first non-whitespace byte its callers have already located.

The result is unchanged because every fact is defined as the helper it
replaces. The two column counts are kept apart rather than unified,
since they have always disagreed: `calc_indentation`, which list
continuation depth is compared against, charges a tab a flat four
columns wherever it sits, while the true column count advances to the
next multiple of four. `LineFacts::trimmed` stays byte-identical to
`line.trim_start()`, Unicode whitespace included, so a marker behind a
non-breaking space is still read the way it was. New unit tests pin
each fact to the scan it replaces, and HTML plus full AST output —
source spans included — was verified identical to the previous revision
across the CommonMark and GFM spec examples, repository documents and
list/quote edge cases under six option profiles.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
